@startuml ShopLite Order Saga Sequence Diagram

title ShopLite Order Saga - Event-Driven Choreography

actor Customer
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Orders Service" as Orders
database "PostgreSQL" as OrdersDB
participant "Outbox\nDispatcher" as Outbox
participant "Kafka" as Kafka
participant "Inventory Service" as Inventory
database "MongoDB" as InventoryDB

== Happy Path: Stock Available ==

Customer -> Gateway: POST /orders\n{items: [{sku:"ABC", qty:2}]}
activate Gateway
Gateway -> Gateway: Validate JWT\n(issuer, aud, exp, scopes)
Gateway -> Orders: Forward request\n+ JWT token
activate Orders

Orders -> Orders: CreateOrderUseCase.execute()
Orders -> OrdersDB: BEGIN TRANSACTION
OrdersDB -> OrdersDB: INSERT INTO orders\n(status='PENDING')
OrdersDB -> OrdersDB: INSERT INTO order_items
OrdersDB -> OrdersDB: INSERT INTO outbox\n(OrderPlaced event)
OrdersDB -> Orders: COMMIT

Orders -> Gateway: 201 {orderId, status:'PENDING'}
Gateway -> Customer: 201 Created
deactivate Gateway

...Background Process...

Outbox -> OrdersDB: SELECT * FROM outbox\nWHERE processed_at IS NULL
OrdersDB -> Outbox: Unprocessed events
Outbox -> Kafka: Publish OrderPlaced\n(topic: orders.placed)
activate Kafka
Outbox -> OrdersDB: UPDATE outbox\nSET processed_at=NOW()

Kafka -> Inventory: OrderPlaced event
deactivate Kafka
activate Inventory

Inventory -> InventoryDB: findOne({_id:'ABC'})
InventoryDB -> Inventory: {available:10, reserved:0}
Inventory -> Inventory: Check: available >= qty?\n(10 >= 2 = true)

Inventory -> InventoryDB: updateOne({_id:'ABC'},\n{$inc: {available:-2, reserved:+2}})
InventoryDB -> InventoryDB: Atomic update\n(available=8, reserved=2)

Inventory -> Kafka: Publish StockReserved\n(topic: inventory.stock-reserved)
activate Kafka
Kafka -> Orders: StockReserved event
deactivate Kafka
deactivate Inventory

activate Orders
Orders -> Orders: ProcessStockEventUseCase\n.processStockReserved()
Orders -> OrdersDB: UPDATE orders\nSET status='CONFIRMED'\nWHERE id=orderId
OrdersDB -> Orders: Updated
Orders -> Orders: Log: Order confirmed
deactivate Orders

note over Customer
  Customer can now query
  GET /orders/{id}
  and see status='CONFIRMED'
end note

== Unhappy Path: Insufficient Stock ==

Customer -> Gateway: POST /orders\n{items: [{sku:"XYZ", qty:100}]}
activate Gateway
Gateway -> Gateway: Validate JWT
Gateway -> Orders: Forward request
activate Orders

Orders -> OrdersDB: BEGIN TRANSACTION
OrdersDB -> OrdersDB: INSERT orders (PENDING)
OrdersDB -> OrdersDB: INSERT outbox (OrderPlaced)
OrdersDB -> Orders: COMMIT
Orders -> Gateway: 201 {orderId, status:'PENDING'}
Gateway -> Customer: 201 Created
deactivate Gateway

Outbox -> OrdersDB: Poll outbox
Outbox -> Kafka: Publish OrderPlaced
activate Kafka
Kafka -> Inventory: OrderPlaced event
deactivate Kafka
activate Inventory

Inventory -> InventoryDB: findOne({_id:'XYZ'})
InventoryDB -> Inventory: {available:5, reserved:0}
Inventory -> Inventory: Check: available >= qty?\n(5 >= 100 = FALSE)

Inventory -> Kafka: Publish StockRejected\n(reason: INSUFFICIENT_STOCK,\ndetails: [{requested:100, available:5}])
activate Kafka
Kafka -> Orders: StockRejected event
deactivate Kafka
deactivate Inventory

activate Orders
Orders -> Orders: ProcessStockEventUseCase\n.processStockRejected()
Orders -> OrdersDB: UPDATE orders\nSET status='CANCELLED'\nWHERE id=orderId
OrdersDB -> Orders: Updated
Orders -> Orders: Log: Order cancelled
deactivate Orders

note over Customer
  Customer queries
  GET /orders/{id}
  and sees status='CANCELLED'
end note

== Idempotency & Reliability ==

note over Orders, Inventory
  **Idempotency**:
  - Each event has unique event-id in headers
  - Consumers track processed event IDs
  - Duplicate events are ignored

  **Outbox Pattern**:
  - Events written to DB in same transaction as business data
  - Background dispatcher publishes reliably
  - At-least-once delivery guaranteed

  **Optimistic Locking**:
  - Orders table has 'version' field
  - MongoDB atomic operations for stock updates
end note

@enduml
